# Dependencies
node_modules/
# also match a node_modules symlink specifically (a symlink is not a
# directory, so the trailing-slash pattern above won't catch it - this
# regressed onto main once already via `git add -A` over a dev symlink)
**/node_modules

# Build output
dist/
.astro/

# Environment
#
# A PATTERN, NOT A LIST. These three were named individually, so `api/.env.bak` - a backup
# somebody made beside a real one - was never ignored and was committed on 31 July 2026 with a
# live JWT signing secret in it. The repository is public.
#
# Every name that starts with `.env` now, and every directory, so a copy made in `api/` or
# `client/` is caught the same way as one at the root. `.env.example` is deliberately excluded
# below, because that one is meant to be tracked.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# ...except the template, which carries no values and exists to be read.
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Prisma
api/dist/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sw?

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Live journey-test harness output. Never committed: these are raw transcripts of
# every check-in in a run - 122,000 lines from one eighteen-ground pass - and on a
# real deployment they would be people's own accounts of their work. The harness
# that produces them IS committed; what it produces is not. The written
# assessment is the deliverable, and it is kept.
api/journey/out/
api/journey/out-cohort/
api/journey/org-sim/out/*.json
api/journey/org-sim/out-paid/
api/journey/org-sim/out-verify/

# TypeScript incremental build cache - a local artifact, not source.
# It was tracked, so every typecheck showed up as a file change in every diff.
*.tsbuildinfo
.vercel

# Journey drivers written to run a whole setup end to end. Scratch, not product.
#
# `api/journey/*` rather than `api/journey/`, and the difference is the whole section below.
# A trailing slash excludes the DIRECTORY, and git will not look inside an excluded directory,
# so not one of the `!` lines under here did anything - `the-real-gate` and `two-scenarios`
# survived only because they were already tracked, and a new file in either would have been
# ignored in silence, which is the exact thing those lines were written to prevent.
api/journey/*

# EXCEPT THE TWO THAT DEFINE DONE, which are not scratch and were one `rm` from gone.
#
# `the-real-gate` drives a lead's actual path - entry chat, a workplan into Context, targets, three
# rounds, the close - and prints what a person reads at each stage. It is the acceptance standard:
# "the conversation has to be worthwhile and make sense from start to close, the reports have to
# make sense, and the lead has to feel they are tracking what they need accurately." It found five
# defects that 1,715 green structural checks could not see.
#
# `two-scenarios` is the regression net underneath it: every situation, every surface, after every
# round.
#
# The last thing this repo lost to an ignore rule was the report templates - nine surfaces had been
# built against a file nobody could open any more, and rebuilding it from memory took a night. A
# thing the team's standard depends on does not live outside the repo.
!api/journey/the-real-gate/
!api/journey/two-scenarios/

# HOW STEADY PATTERNS ARE ACROSS RUNS (decision 57, item 4). Read-only: reads existing run folders
# under api/journey/all-24/ (which stay out, as always - see below) and writes nothing back.
!api/journey/pattern-steadiness.ts
!api/journey/pattern-steadiness.spec.ts

# THE LIVE PROOF THAT ASK GROUNDWORK SAVES THE SAME THING THE OLD CONTEXT CHAT DOES (decision 50,
# piece 2, step (c)). Local-only and it refuses to run against anything else - see the file itself.
!api/journey/context-chat-equivalence.ts
# Reads a stored run's conversations twice through the pattern detector; writes nothing to the database.
!api/journey/the-detector-read-twice.ts
!api/journey/how-steady-each-way-is.py
!api/journey/how-steady-each-way-is-2.py
!api/journey/the-four-live-checks.ts

# AND THE FOUR SEEDS THE SCREENS WORKSPACE LOADS (requests 154, 155 and the review company,
# 5-6 October 2026). They were written, committed and reported as done, and not one of them was in
# the commit: `git add -A api/journey` on an ignored path does nothing and says nothing, so three
# requests were answered with instructions pointing at files that existed on one computer only.
# The screens workspace found it (request 156), which is the second time in two weeks this rule has
# hidden a file somebody else needed.
!api/journey/a-database-on-this-computer.ts
!api/journey/seed-the-suites-for-the-screens.ts
!api/journey/seed-a-company-for-review.ts
!api/journey/seed-an-anchor-check-in.ts
!api/journey/seed-a-hundred-check-ins.ts

# THE ANCHOR JOURNEY (anchor piece 35). Its reader rules live in api/src/modules/board/the-anchor-readers.ts, because
# nothing in api/src may import from outside api/src. Read-only, and it refuses anything that is not this computer.
!api/journey/anchor/
api/journey/anchor/*
!api/journey/anchor/walk-the-anchor-as-each-reader.ts
!api/journey/anchor/walk-the-anchor-as-each-reader.spec.ts

# AND THE 24-SCENARIO RUNNER, for the same reason, asked for by the screens workspace on
# 26 September 2026: `api/journey/all-24/` only existed on one computer, so the other workspace
# could not run the scenarios or the scorer - and no task on either list may be ticked without
# them. The right answers themselves live here too, in `theDecision` on each scenario.
#
# SOURCE ONLY. Every run writes a folder of transcripts beside these files, and those stay out:
# the directory is re-ignored and the files are named one at a time.
!api/journey/all-24/
api/journey/all-24/*
!api/journey/all-24/run.ts
!api/journey/all-24/scenarios.ts
!api/journey/all-24/refresh.ts
!api/journey/the-suite/
api/journey/the-suite/*
!api/journey/the-suite/run.ts
!api/journey/the-suite/scenarios.ts

# Audit and fix-plan working notes. Written while reading the product, kept on disk, never in a PR:
# they are how the work was decided, not the work. The product docs (api-terms, edge-protection)
# stay tracked - those are things the product itself points at.
docs/audit/

# The prototype screens: 34MB of screenshots, kept on this computer and out of git.
# They are reference for building, not part of the product, and git history is the wrong
# place for a folder of images that will be replaced wholesale each time it is redrawn.
docs/prototype/

# The made-up people the browser user journeys share while they run (e2e/user-journeys-world.ts).
e2e/.user-journeys-world.json
